<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jehoahaz of Judah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">609 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jehoahaz was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> for three months in 609 BCE, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah">Josiah</a>. After Josiah was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-megiddo">Megiddo</a> the people of the land made Jehoahaz king, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/necho-ii">Necho II</a> deposed him and took him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, where he died. Necho installed his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehoiakim">Jehoiakim</a> in his place as an Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jehoahaz-of-judah.jpg" alt="Jehoahaz of Judah" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bartolomeo Gajus · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joacaz-Jehoahaz_of_Judah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
